### Validate Token Examples
### IMPORTANT: The validate-token endpoint is NOT publicly accessible!
### It's only accessible by the Gateway middleware with internal API key.
### Only the login endpoint is public.

### 1. Login first to get a token (InHouse provider example) - PUBLIC ENDPOINT
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. ❌ DIRECT ACCESS TO VALIDATE-TOKEN IS FORBIDDEN
### This will return 403 Forbidden because validate-token is internal only
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/validate-token
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 3. ✅ GATEWAY ACCESS (how it actually works)
### The Gateway middleware calls validate-token internally with API key
### Users should call protected endpoints through the Gateway:
GET https://localhost:5000/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 4. Example with SAML token (replace with actual SAML assertion) - PUBLIC ENDPOINT
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "samlAssertion": "PHNhbWw6QXNzZXJ0aW9uIC4uLg=="
}

### 5. Example with OAuth token (replace with actual OAuth code) - PUBLIC ENDPOINT
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "oAuthCode": "auth_code_12345",
  "extraParameters": {
    "client_id": "your_client_id",
    "redirect_uri": "https://your-app.com/callback"
  }
}

### 6. Example with OIDC token (replace with actual ID token) - PUBLIC ENDPOINT
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idToken": "eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
}

### 7. Example with JWT bearer token (replace with actual JWT) - PUBLIC ENDPOINT
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bearerToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
}

### 8. ❌ SECURITY TESTS - These should all fail with 403 Forbidden

# Missing API key - should return 403
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/validate-token
Authorization: Bearer valid-token-here

# Invalid API key - should return 403
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/validate-token
Authorization: Bearer valid-token-here
X-Internal-API-Key: invalid-key

# Direct access through Gateway (should also be blocked)
POST https://localhost:5000/api/auth/validate-token
Authorization: Bearer valid-token-here

### 9. ✅ CORRECT USAGE PATTERN
### Users authenticate via login, then use tokens for protected resources through Gateway

# Step 1: Login to get token
POST https://localhost:5001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "password123"
}

# Step 2: Use token for protected resources (Gateway handles validation internally)
GET https://localhost:5000/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer <token-from-step-1>

### SECURITY ARCHITECTURE:
# 1. Only /api/auth/login is publicly accessible
# 2. /api/auth/validate-token is INTERNAL ONLY (Gateway ↔ Identity)
# 3. All other endpoints go through Gateway with token validation
# 4. Gateway adds user context headers for downstream services

### Expected Response for Direct validate-token Access:
# {
#   "errorCode": "FORBIDDEN",
#   "errorMessage": "This endpoint is only accessible by the Gateway"
# }